  "metadata": {
    "title": "MALO (major adverse liver outcome) definition in ESPRESSO",
    "source": "ESPRESSO Study; MALO_definitions_ESPRESSO_261118.docx",
    "version": "2026-11-18",
    "last_updated": "2026-11-18",
    "description": "Five-point composite: the first occurrence of any of compensated cirrhosis, decompensated cirrhosis, hepatocellular carcinoma, liver transplantation or liver-related death. Components 4 and 5 are defined in the separate liver_transplant and liver_related_death code lists.",
    "used_in": [
      "Close to the definition in Yao et al on celiac disease and chronic liver disease (PMID 40093397), with the changes listed in note M1"
    ],
